{"title":"GATE 2027-Subjectwise Test- 12 (Electromagnetic Fields)","fileName":"041_GATE 2027-Subjectwise Test- 12 (Electromagnetic Fields).html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2027 Online Test Series - Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":5400,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Two infinite line charges, each having linear charge density +5 &mu;C/m, are placed parallel to the z-axis at (2,0) m and (-2,0) m. The magnitude of the electric field at the origin is:</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>22.5 &times; 10<sup>3</sup> V/m</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>45 &times; 10<sup>3</sup> V/m</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>90 &times; 10<sup>3</sup> V/m</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>0</p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>The fields due to the two identical positive line charges at the origin are equal in magnitude and opposite in direction.<br />Therefore, E<sub>net</sub> = 0</p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A long solid cylindrical conductor of radius R carries a uniformly distributed current I. Which statements are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>Magnetic field inside increases linearly with radius.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>Magnetic field outside varies as 1/r.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>Magnetic field is maximum at the conductor surface.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>Magnetic field inside is constant.</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/9ab29e9423821985b703ea5d9022bb96d8388a7d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"multi | Marks +1"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The magnetic dipole moment of a circuit formed by the triangular loop shown below, will be</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/2e6cd685f8eecefdc096f10adc65208c8d5d690b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/373666ed99508bd99efee5f21a509d4dac0f34f5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/bcf5fc5226cfcab375b04727f88b31e959ec9978.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/af553d162edb65c4816e4ce19d0efe8668a0e571.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/dba8037ae694ec9002a2d975cd69882ee07ea52f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/cd2584937ee3531737ededf4042e3374e42e292b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/902011d72e0ab5244407adafe9e8558626c43478.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":4,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A conducting spherical shell has inner radius 4 cm and outer radius 6 cm. A point charge of 10 nC is placed at the center. Find the electric field magnitude at a point 5 cm from the center.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0","high":"0"},"solution":"<p>The point lies inside the conducting material. In electrostatic equilibrium, the electric field inside a conductor is zero.</p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":5,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/a0c05f5fc4117c7ee05bc4398a7503cef27db815.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"12.2","high":"12.7"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/9394352c115973db0575c51171c15b8f53962caa.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/886dfed67d299e285d56c1e86559b55ee95d170d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-1","high":"-0.9"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/07ecd5920021f70d752451a463575b80142b93f3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The electric field intensity in polystyrenes (&epsilon;<sub>r</sub> = 2.55) filling the space between the plates of a parallel plate capacitor is 10 kV/m. The distance between the plates is 1.5 mm. The surface charge density of free charge on the plates is _________ (&mu;C/m<sup>2</sup>).</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.21","high":"0.25"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/e82c26eb9dfd984c48547fcab74fb6cd0c610b80.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A circuit has 2000 turns enclosing a magnetic circuit 30 cm<sup>2</sup> in section. A current of 5 A in the circuit produces a field of flux density 1(Tesla) and when current is doubled, flux density increases only by 50%. The mean value of inductance of the circuit between 5 A and 10 A is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>0.4 H</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>0.5 H</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>0.6 H</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>0.7 H</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/e92ddb77eba61a5178e3208cab2c7b76b0260580.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/80c38e43b26a477cfd25b163f775fee90d961a9c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>&ndash;20 &mu;C</p></d