>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/d4f636d19549547408403c90f1703502e94d1c7f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/b45b4a7193c41ed82fc86e62e359acf23adbbf4d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/c109b886398160a3ea8078f8d0fe7c78560453c4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":12,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A point charge Q = 30 nC is located at the origin in Cartesian coordinates. The magnitude of electric flux density <img src=\"/media/2b2ba4dfc17c70ba401a9c77aa41aea18b1a8af9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" />at (1, 3, &ndash;4) m is</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"91.6","high":"91.99"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/52b5bd42d5bbc257c8598fb0f19502dc5467b96d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>In cylindrical coordinates, V = 0, at &rho; = 2 m and V = 60 V at &rho; = 5 m due to charge distribution </p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/81338e7156ac7cfe5a5485959a0c54f1269e0058.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/940bed8ed721eaaa69d6d999cf3610def914338c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/d907fde79b05f5a85ebe6034a86202b45c3ccfe2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/03f3b767b852aab2c8fae2e01bc6fc47b1a2559c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/2230abd3497bcb31916d2c60ecec783be9371f88.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/0736d0540028404e697d64f56098a3c7368e6582.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/2fcafd773f369de9eac290559e89988b69e7fa5a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":14,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>An electron (q<sub>1</sub>) is moving in free space with 105 m/sec towards a stationary electron (q<sub>2</sub>) at some distance. The closest distance that this moving electron can approach stationary electron before the repulsive force diverts its path is ________ 10<sup>&ndash;8 </sup>m. (Answer upto 2 decimal places).<br />(Assume, electron mass, m = 9.11 &times; 10<sup>&ndash;31</sup> kg, charge q = &ndash;1.6 &times; 10<sup>&ndash;19</sup> C and permittivity,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/92baed997f432ff5d3bb463aac18d933996098cd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"5","high":"5.1"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/f823526506c398ad69592e08e290d76ad1c307bc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/41a6709f3ed10abfdf5cdb70251c4f19d255ae08.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +2"},{"qnum":15,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A stationary 10 turn square coil of 1 metre-side is situated with its lower left corner coincident with the origin and with sides x<sub>1</sub> and y<sub>1</sub> along x-axis and y-axis. If the field B is normal to the plane of coil and has its amplitude given by</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/928b4d861f8f73b50b473abcde2dca49eb32c48b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The rms value of emf induced in the coil if B varies harmonically at a frequency of 1 kHz</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>14 kV</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>18 kV</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>22 kV</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>28 kV</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/4440c811682c3e5091cd521b3af23edaf5ab2636.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/b4e08df043ea1f10c94d6a9e3f88709cecfeffc6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/2d06b11290a315d0e8faecce5ec668dc4fbdcee7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/f1d405fc1ea912f152f89cf8ecdfe37506d02594.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/7f45255ffe7d678984669b4893f2d84dd7cad90d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/8a893e280b65db21c8cf71be6651c9c3ab2942b9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/8bb19eabdde41dc94d68545e9fb4198e3c07d7f7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":17,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A positively charged circular ring with charge density 5 nC/m and radius 5 m. At what distance from its centre the electric field will be maximum ________ m. (rounded up to two decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3.52","high":"3.54"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/41ea1ac2a70582dc3e8982efc96c7a3035599af4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":18,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Half of the space between the plates of a parallel plate capacitor is filled with a dielectric material of dielectric constant K. The remaining half contains air as shown in figure. The capacitor is now given a charge Q. Then</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/8d7db0b603786e4c5e683194d9f96cb70d35aaf1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>Electric field in the dielectric region is higher than air filled region.</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>Charged densities of air filled and dielectric region are equal.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>Plate towards air-filled part will have charge <img src=\"/media/d4616ac523df560979a6301c49c379bdcc42fa12.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>Capacitance of the capacitor shown in figure is <img src=\"/media/34bf25a8b603448b98a818b31f042e9f8d561e32.png\" loading=\"lazy\" />where C<sub>0</sub> is capacitance of same<br />capacitor without dielectric.</p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/124b955fa07510f5810f960bd265f1477cfd6134.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"multi | Marks +2"},{"qnum":19,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/33b064341fc10828f5721a4ad250d8d58c2129d6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>&ndash;8.255 V</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>&ndash;6.255 V</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>11.250 V</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>&ndash;20.25 V</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/c88d61eee12221143f09f955845b45b429abc6c0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/8a85b519c332bd9990b053150bf381df760c627a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":20,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A solid conducting sphere having charge density 25 nC/m and radius 5 cm. Calculate the potential at a distance 2 mm from the centre of sphere is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>3.53 V</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>5.329 V</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>9.125 V</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>0.0078 V</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"na