edia/31085a3d3e8c195030716038ab8eb7d6fa1234f4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":23,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/d9df35d0a32a1622bba53db16168fd6fc990511d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/15091130373d60e096f23383355ebf8affd2c638.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/1a185c1e267d24324e378cdbd61e3532b80ab316.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/a3b310c093842beacbe626313003244ebdd47ab9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/d7a87a7386859ebc854d30360cb830f62ff9c026.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/12410a14f520dbec3aadc084977023080963120b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/b200b088400085d1f08f36cbed25778f21f3a12b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":24,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following statements about equipotential surface and choose the correct statements:</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>Work done by tangential component of E-field on equipotential surface is zero.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>Work done by normal component of E-field on equipotential surface is zero.</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>E-field and equipotential surface intersect each other at 90&deg;.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>Normal component of E-field on equipotential surface is zero.</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>Properties of Equipotential surface (EPS)<br />(i) Tangential component of E-field on EPS is zero.<br />(ii) Normal c